ss":"lord of the land"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பிரியா","parts":[{"text":"பிரி","lemma":"பிரி","gloss":"separate"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ஆ","gloss":"negative relative participle"}],"gloss":"inseparable"},{"surface":"நண்பினர்","parts":[{"text":"நண்பு","lemma":"நண்பு","gloss":"friendship"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"possessive"},{"text":"அர்","lemma":"அர்","gloss":"they (plural/honorific)"}],"gloss":"friends"},{"surface":"இருவரும்","parts":[{"text":"இருவர்","lemma":"இருவர்","gloss":"two people"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"both"}],"gloss":"both of them"},{"surface":"என்னும்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"say"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"relative participle"}],"gloss":"saying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அலரதற்கு","parts":[{"text":"அலரதற்கு","lemma":"அலரதற்கு","gloss":"for that gossip"}],"gloss":"for that gossip","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அஞ்சினன்","parts":[{"text":"அஞ்சு","lemma":"அஞ்சு","gloss":"fear"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"past tense"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"அன்","gloss":"he (masculine singular)"}],"gloss":"he feared"},{"surface":"கொல்லோ","parts":[{"text":"கொல்","lemma":"கொல்","gloss":"particle of doubt"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ஓ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"perhaps?"},{"surface":"பலருடன்","parts":[{"text":"பலர்","lemma":"பலர்","gloss":"many people"},{"text":"உடன்","lemma":"உடன்","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with many people"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"துஞ்சூர்","parts":[{"text":"துஞ்சு","lemma":"துஞ்சு","gloss":"sleep"},{"text":"ஊர்","lemma":"ஊர்","gloss":"town"}],"gloss":"sleeping town"},{"surface":"யாமத்தானும்","parts":[{"text":"யாமத்தானும்","lemma":"யாமத்தானும்","gloss":"even at midnight"}],"gloss":"even at midnight","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நெஞ்சத்து","parts":[{"text":"நெஞ்சத்து","lemma":"நெஞ்சத்து","gloss":"of the heart"}],"gloss":"of the heart","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அல்லது","parts":[{"text":"அல்","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"not"},{"text":"அது","lemma":"அது","gloss":"that"}],"gloss":"except"},{"surface":"வரவு","parts":[{"text":"வரவு","lemma":"வரவு","gloss":"coming"}],"gloss":"coming","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அறியானே","parts":[{"text":"அறியானே","lemma":"அறியானே","gloss":"he does not know how to come"}],"gloss":"he does not know how to come","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Please tell, friend, is that fitting? Is it not? / Even suffering this difficult sorrow, we cannot bear; on top of this, / dying, even more than that, we fear. / Alas! Still, the lord of the good mountain land, / 'They both are inseparable friends,' saying, / did he fear that gossip? With many people / in the sleeping town, even at midnight, my / except in my heart, he does not know how to come!","translation":"Tell me, my friend, is this fair? It is not. We cannot bear to suffer this deep sorrow. And on top of this, we fear dying even more. Alas! Still, the lord of the good mountain land—did he fear the gossip that says, 'Those two are inseparable friends'? Even at midnight, when the whole town is asleep with many others, he does not know how to come anywhere except into my heart!","modern":"தோழியே! நீ சொல்வது தகுதியானதா? இல்லை. இந்த அரிய துன்பத்தைத் தாங்கிக் கொள்ள எம்மால் இயலவில்லை. இதற்கு மேலாக, இறந்து போவதைக் காட்டிலும் நாங்கள் அஞ்சுகிறோம். ஐயோ! இன்னமும் அந்த நல்ல மலைநாடன், 'இவர்கள் இருவரும் பிரியாத நண்பர்கள்' என்று ஊரார் பேசும் அலருக்கு அஞ்சினானோ? எல்லாரும் உறங்கும் நள்ளிரவிலும் கூட, அவன் என் நெஞ்சத்தைத் தவிர வேறு எங்கும் வரத் தெரியாதவனாக இருக்கிறானே!","explanation":"The heroine is speaking to her close friend when the hero delays his arrival for marriage, leaving her in deep distress. She laments that she cannot bear the pain of separation and fears death even more. She wonders if the hero is staying away because he fears the town's gossip about their inseparable bond. She points out that even at midnight, when the entire town is asleep and there is no danger of being seen, he only appears in her thoughts and does not come to meet her in reality. This poem belongs to the Kuriñci tiṇai, where the quietness of the midnight town contrasts with the heroine's restless heart. Key words include 'அருந்துயர்' (difficult sorrow), 'பெரும்பிறிதாகல்' (death), and 'அலர்' (gossip).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.9],[0.9,2.0],[2.0,2.0],[2.0,3.0],[3.3,3.62],[3.7,4.1],[4.1,4.8],[4.8,5.4],[5.4,6.0],[6.0,6.6],[6.6,6.9],[6.9,6.9],[6.9,8.4],[8.4,8.9],[8.9,9.3],[9.3,9.83],[9.97,10.5],[10.5,11.0],[11.0,11.3],[11.3,11.3],[11.3,12.3],[12.3,12.7],[12.7,13.2],[13.33,13.6],[13.73,14.4],[14.4,14.9],[14.9,15.35],[15.35,15.41],[15.41,15.41],[15.41,15.6]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.4],[1.47,1.93],[2.0,2.3],[2.3,3.6],[3.6,4.3],[4.3,4.86],[5.0,5.8],[5.8,6.4],[6.4,7.0],[7.0,7.7],[7.7,8.0],[8.0,8.0],[8.0,9.2],[9.2,10.3],[10.3,10.8],[10.8,11.6],[11.6,12.4],[12.4,12.9],[12.9,13.3],[13.3,14.91],[14.91,15.09],[15.09,15.43],[15.6,17.27],[17.27,17.27],[17.27,17.27],[17.27,18.3],[18.3,19.0],[19.0,19.1],[19.1,19.1],[19.1,19.4]]}}